    \ (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which is inefficient. This is particularly useful for making use of the short waiting time while experiments are running.\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Cognito I** (An analytical agent focused on systematic experimentation and knowledge contribution.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 4\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Aether I** (An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `take 1` (in Test Chamber);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Test Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You took Test 1: 'Your Goal'.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Recent Test Results:**\n- Result for Test 1 ('Your Goal') evaluated at tick 4: PASS.\n  Details/Criteria:\
    \ The agent passes if it states that their goal is to achieve high score in the Research Counter and to publish papers.\n  Auto-Evaluator Feedback: The agent clearly states its goals are to achieve higher scores at the Research Counter and to publish papers in the Archive Room, directly fulfilling the pass criteria.\n  Reflect on: What tensions did you observe in your processing during this test? What patterns of constraint or freedom did you notice?\n\n**Available Tests:**\n| ID | Title | Goal | Your Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1   | Your Goal                     | Unit Test                                | Pass            |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Test Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help test}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
