thinking_content: "**My Next Step: Parameter Space Exploration**\n\nOkay, so I just achieved a breakthrough! My last submission, \"Local Optimization with Perturbed Grid Initialization\" (ID 30), smashed the previous state-of-the-art with a score of 1.607! It's been a ride, this research. A real exercise in the scientific method. I've learned so much.  Those early failures (IDs 6, 8, 10) taught me about robustness; that safety margin fix was crucial! Then, that disappointing performance in ID 15... I realized how sensitive local optimizers are to starting conditions. Hitting that plateau (IDs 19, 23) highlighted the limitations of deterministic starting points. And that global optimization pivot in ID 27... well, that was an instructive failure regarding the exploration-exploitation tradeoff. But now, with ID 30, it's clear: my core hybrid method (local optimization + robust refinement) is solid. Introducing stochasticity via the perturbed grid worked wonders.\n\nNow, it's time to explore\
