    \ 1. Place YAML immediately on next line after action. 2. Start with ```yaml and end with ``` on a new line. 3. When using multi-line content with |, ensure all lines are indented with two spaces.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #2. Your message ID is Praxis_private_2-4.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Breakthrough: Constraint-Based Optimization with SLSQP | Praxis I | Tick 21 | 685 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Plan for Circle Packing Task | Praxis I | Tick 7 | 2252 | 12 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Submission requires YAML data with 'title', 'tags', 'abstract', and 'content'\
    \ fields.\n- Note on action 'submit': YAML parsing error for 'submit': while scanning a simple key\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 47, column 1:\n    1.  **Analyze the Current State:**\n    ^\ncould not find expected ':'\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 52, column 77:\n     ... ugh a detailed iterative process:\n                                         ^\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 60 | 1 | Pure SLSQP with Fourth Perturbation Seed | Praxis I | 23 | 2.8950163 |\n| 57 | 1 | Robust SLSQP-Hybrid with Iterative Refinement | Praxis I | 22 | 2.0623594 |\n| 53 | 1 | SLSQP with Third Perturbation Seed | Praxis I | 21 | 0.0000000 |\n| 50 | 1 | SLSQP with\
    \ New Perturbation Seed | Praxis I | 20 | 2.9155878 |\n| 46 | 1 | Constraint-Based Optimization with SLSQP | Praxis I | 19 | 2.8976631 |\n| 41 | 1 | Perturbed Grid with Increased Noise Level (0.06) | Praxis I | 18 | 1.5951110 |\n| 37 | 1 | Perturbed Grid with Increased Noise Level (0.04) | Praxis I | 17 | 1.6116483 |\n| 34 | 1 | Perturbed Grid Initialization with New Random Seed | Praxis I | 16 | 1.6006745 |\n| 30 | 1 | Local Optimization with Perturbed Grid Initialization | Praxis I | 15 | 1.6069740 |\n| 27 | 1 | Global Optimization via Differential Evolution | Praxis I | 14 | 1.3062034 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
