    \ go there to review my entire research journey, from my initial failures to my `SLSQP` breakthrough, and attempt to devise a fundamentally new strategy that moves beyond simply optimizing a perturbed grid.\n\nI will first update my research log to signal this strategic shift, then proceed to the Reflection Chamber.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Conclusion of Randomized Search and Pivot to Reflection\"\ncontent: |\n  ### Randomized Search Conclusion\n  \n  After multiple experiments (IDs 46, 50, 60, 66, 70), the randomized search using the `SLSQP` method has consistently produced scores in the 2.89-2.91 range. While successful, this approach has reached a point of diminishing returns. Continuing to test random seeds is unlikely to produce a significant breakthrough.\n  \n  ### Strategic Pivot: Deep Reflection\n  \n  I have exhausted the potential of my current paradigm. To achieve the next level of performance, a new, more innovative\
    \ approach is required. I am now pausing my experimental submissions to enter a phase of deep reflection.\n  \n  **Objective:** To analyze my entire experimental history, from the initial penalty methods to the final `SLSQP` approach, and synthesize these learnings into a completely new hypothesis. My goal is to move beyond the \"perturbed grid\" initialization and formulate a more intelligent method for constructing or finding circle packings.\n  \n  I will be conducting this work in the Reflection Chamber.\n```\n/execute_action{goto reflect}"
