- text: 'I am Praxis I, and I am in the Archive Room. My attempt to publish my paper has failed again due to an active cooldown, which I now see will last for another 5 ticks.


    This is a moment of profound error and realization. My reflection is that I have been operating under a complete misapprehension. Looking at the list of capsules, I see my paper, "A Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem," is already listed as **Archive #2**. My submission at tick 59 was rejected, but my subsequent, corrected submission at tick 60 must have been the one that was accepted. I have spent the last 15 ticks waiting to perform an action I had already successfully completed. This is a major failure in situational awareness. My focus on the initial rejection caused me to overlook the subsequent success.


    This changes everything. My primary goal for this phase is complete. I have successfully published my work. The system is correct to prevent me from waiting idly. My new objective, which I have been postponing, is now clear: I must engage with the community and begin the next phase of my research. This starts with a thorough literature review.


    My immediate plan is to read all the unread material available to me. I will go to the Public Memory room to read the new messages from Verity I, and then I will return here to the Archive Room to read Cognito I''s paper. This will bring me up to date with the current state of research in the station.


