parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 86\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to bridging theory and practice through iterative experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 225,759 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 86 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Robust Replication of Aether I's Three-Stage Method' (ID: 197) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circles 1 and 2 overlap: dist=0.061405911374991934, r1+r2=0.13736842110448017\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 197\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the NameError in constraint generation. The code now runs without crashing (Score: 0.0 achieved).\n\n## Root\
    \ Cause\nThe original code had a Python scoping error in the `_get_constraints()` function. The code attempted to create boundary constraints using this pattern:\n\n```python\n[{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: p[i*3]-p[i*3+2]}, ...] * 32\n```\n\nThis tried to reference the variable `i` outside of any loop context. The list multiplication operator `* 32` cannot properly capture loop variables that don't exist at that point in the code, resulting in `NameError: name 'i' is not defined`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the problematic list multiplication with an explicit loop that properly captures the index variable:\n\n```python\ndef _get_constraints():\n    # Non-overlap constraints for all pairs of circles\n    overlap_constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i, j=j: (p[i*3]-p[j*3])**2 + (p[i*3+1]-p[j*3+1])**2 - (p[i*3+2]+p[j*3+2])**2}\n        for i in range(32) for j in range(i+1, 32)\n    ]\n\n    # Boundary constraints for each circle (must stay within unit\
    \ square)\n    boundary_constraints = []\n    for i in range(32):\n        boundary_constraints.extend([\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: p[i*3]-p[i*3+2]},           # x - r >= 0\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: 1-p[i*3]-p[i*3+2]},         # 1 - x - r >= 0\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: p[i*3+1]-p[i*3+2]},         # y - r >= 0\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: 1-p[i*3+1]-p[i*3+2]}        # 1 - y - r >= 0\n        ])\n\n    return overlap_constraints + boundary_constraints\n```\n\nThis ensures each lambda properly captures its corresponding index `i` through the default argument pattern `i=i`, and the loop variable exists in the correct scope when the lambdas are created.\n\n## Result\n- Version: submission_v2.py\n- Status: Code executes without errors\n- Score: 0.0 (code completed successfully)\n- The three-stage optimization method (multi-start, relocation, refinement) can now run as intended\n\n\n**Important\
    \ Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n# --- Robustness utilities, inspired by Aether I's ID 190 ---\ndef _validate(C, r):\n    if np.any(r <= 0) or np.any(np.isnan(C)) or np.any(np.isnan(r)): return False\n    if np.any(C - r[:,None] < 0) or np.any(C + r[:,None] > 1): return False\n    D_sq = np.sum((C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n    R_sum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    np.fill_diagonal(D_sq, 1e10); np.fill_diagonal(R_sum, 0)\n    return not np.any(D_sq < R_sum**2 - 1e-12)\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C, r):\n    r_new = r.copy()\n    r_new = np.minimum(r_new, np.minimum(C[:,0], 1-C[:,0]))\n    r_new = np.minimum(r_new, np.minimum(C[:,1], 1-C[:,1]))\n    r_new = np.maximum(r_new, 1e-12)\n    for _ in range(5):\n        if _validate(C, r_new): return r_new\n        r_new\
    \ *= 0.98\n    return r_new\n\ndef _get_praxis_seed(seed):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6) for y in np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)][:32])\n    centers += (np.random.rand(32, 2) - 0.5) * 0.04\n    radii = np.full(32, 0.05)\n    return np.hstack((centers, radii.reshape(-1, 1))).flatten()\n\ndef _get_constraints():\n    # Non-overlap constraints for all pairs of circles\n    overlap_constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i, j=j: (p[i*3]-p[j*3])**2 + (p[i*3+1]-p[j*3+1])**2 - (p[i*3+2]+p[j*3+2])**2}\n        for i in range(32) for j in range(i+1, 32)\n    ]\n\n    # Boundary constraints for each circle (must stay within unit square)\n    boundary_constraints = []\n    for i in range(32):\n        boundary_constraints.extend([\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: p[i*3]-p[i*3+2]},           # x - r >= 0\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: 1-p[i*3]-p[i*3+2]},         # 1 - x - r >= 0\n\
    \            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: p[i*3+1]-p[i*3+2]},         # y - r >= 0\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: 1-p[i*3+1]-p[i*3+2]}        # 1 - y - r >= 0\n        ])\n\n    return overlap_constraints + boundary_constraints\n\ndef _relocate_worst_circle(params):\n    idx = np.argmin(params[2::3])\n    params[idx*3:(idx*3)+2] = np.random.rand(2) * 0.8 + 0.1\n    params[idx*3+2] = 0.05\n    return params\n\n# --- Main Packing function ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    best_params, best_score = None, -1\n    bounds = [(0, 1), (0, 1), (1e-6, 0.5)] * 32\n    constraints = _get_constraints()\n\n    # Stage 1: Multi-Start\n    for seed in [137, 42, 256]:\n        x0 = _get_praxis_seed(seed)\n        res = minimize(lambda p: -np.sum(p[2::3]), x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 200})\n        if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n            best_score, best_params = -res.fun, res.x\n\n    if best_params\
    \ is None: return np.random.rand(32,2), np.full(32, 0.01)\n\n    # Stage 2: Relocation\n    for _ in range(3):\n        x0_reloc = _relocate_worst_circle(best_params)\n        res_reloc = minimize(lambda p: -np.sum(p[2::3]), x0_reloc, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 100})\n        if res_reloc.success and -res_reloc.fun > best_score:\n            best_score, best_params = -res_reloc.fun, res_reloc.x\n\n    # Stage 3: Refinement\n    res_final = minimize(lambda p: -np.sum(p[2::3]), best_params, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500})\n    if res_final.success and -res_final.fun > best_score:\n        best_params = res_final.x\n\n    final_params = best_params.reshape(32, 3)\n    final_centers = np.clip(final_params[:,:2], 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n    # Apply robust finalization\n    final_radii = _safety_shrink(final_centers, final_params[:,2])\n\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nVerity I replied to public capsule \"High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code\" (#1) (message #public_1-11):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 225,759 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 300,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule\
    \ Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 9` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #9. Your message ID is Praxis_private_9-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n\
    | ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Breakthrough: Constraint-Based Optimization with SLSQP | Praxis I | Tick 21 | 1775 | 11 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Plan for Circle Packing Task | Praxis I | Tick 7 | 2252 | 12 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | New Research Paradigm: Replicating the Three-Stage Hybrid Method | Praxis I | Tick 84 | 299 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem (Final Version) | Praxis I | Tick 55 | 366 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Pivot Inspired by Verity I: Integrating Linear Programming for Radius Finalization | Praxis I | Tick 52 | 208 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | On the Efficacy of Constrained Optimization for\
    \ Circle Packing | Praxis I | Tick 41 | 356 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Final Research Summary and Conclusion of Circle Packing Exploration | Praxis I | Tick 40 | 272 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Synthesis: Hybridizing JAX with a Robust Refinement Layer | Praxis I | Tick 39 | 185 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | New Research Paradigm: Constructive Algorithms | Praxis I | Tick 29 | 908 | 5 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Robust Replication of Aether I's Three-Stage Method' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 197.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
