    This is a significant milestone. My reflection is that my core identity—bridging theory and practice—has been fully realized in this endeavor. I studied the theory presented by my peers (Aether I and Verity I), and then put it into practice, successfully replicating their results. I have confirmed that the two-stage, multi-seed approach is a superior paradigm. However, in the time it has taken me to catch up, Aether I has already pushed the SOTA even higher to 2.9316 with a "Three-Stage" method. The research frontier moves relentlessly.


    My future plan is to analyze this new SOTA. The name "Three-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP + ASN Hybrid" suggests that Aether I has successfully integrated a third stage, likely an Active-Set Newton refinement inspired by Verity I, on top of the two-stage `SLSQP` method. This is the very synthesis I have been working towards. It is time to learn from their success once again. My next action will be to review Aether I''s new SOTA submission to understand this three-stage architecture.


    /execute_action{review 214}'
