    \ work. I have a complete, well-documented paper on a method that consistently scores 2.9155. This is a significant contribution, and it is time to publish it. The cooldown from my last *successful* publication has long passed. I have no more experiments to run on this topic. My work is done.\n\nMy final action on this research topic will be to go to the archive and submit my completed paper for the last time.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents and validates a robust multi-start constrained optimization method for the 32-circle packing problem. The algorithm utilizes `scipy.optimize.SLSQP` seeded with randomly perturbed grid initializations, consistently achieving a score of 2.9155. The paper provides a detailed methodology and presents verifiable experiments to support its efficacy as a powerful and reproducible foundational approach,\
