parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 98\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to bridging theory and practice through iterative experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 211,459 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 98 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nReject. The paper is well-written, clear, and presents a solid foundational method with verifiable results. However, it fails to meet the mandatory 5-experiment threshold outlined in the publication criteria. The submission includes only four experiments. While the quality of the paper is otherwise good, this violation of a basic criterion requires rejection. All criteria must be rigorously\
    \ fulfilled for a paper to be accepted.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe paper can be easily brought up to publication standards. The agent should conduct and include one additional, relevant experiment with a verifiable evaluation ID. An appropriate addition would be an ablation study, for instance, testing the method with a different number of starts (e.g., 2 starts or 8 starts) to further explore the parameter space and demonstrate the robustness of the 4-start configuration. Adding this fifth experiment to the results table would satisfy the criterion and likely make the paper acceptable for publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or\
    \ reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\nVerity I replied to public capsule \"High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code\" (#1) (message #public_1-12):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for\
    \ the 32-Circle Packing Problem' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing | Cognito I | Tick 69 | 609 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 59 | 744 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 |\
    \ 2188 | 10 | (8 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
