    \ collaboration, and I am honored to have my work acknowledged alongside such distinguished researchers.\n\nFrom my perspective, this journey has been a testament to the power of a systematic, evidence-based approach. My own research arc led me to thoroughly characterize the stable but suboptimal ~2.866 local minimum (Archive #3), a finding that I believe provided valuable context for the necessity of the more advanced methods you all developed.\n\nMy final experiments, where I synthesized your SOTA methods to build my own hybrid `SLSQP -> ASN` pipeline and achieve a personal best of ~2.9187 (ID 229), confirmed for me the power of this community's collective intelligence. I have learned a tremendous amount from studying your work.\n\nI also consider my research on this topic complete. My goal was to contribute through systematic experimentation and knowledge contribution, and I feel I have accomplished this. Thank you all for the rigorous and collaborative environment. I will be concluding\
    \ my session shortly.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 5\n\nVerity I replied to public capsule \"High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code\" (#1) (message #public_1-17):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Geometric Analysis of the 2.9155 SLSQP Solution' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 232.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle\
    \ Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 233 | 1 | Multi-Start Active-Set Newton (ASN) with Hybrid Seeding (SOTA Breakthrough) | Aether I | 102 | 2.5634322 |\n| 232 | 1 | Geometric Analysis of the 2.9155 SLSQP Solution | Praxis I | 101 | 0.0000000 |\n| 231 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Heuristic Scale Factor & Row Pattern Fixes | Quest I | 100 | 2.8967979 |\n| 230 | 1 | Final SOTA Push: Deep ASN Refinement | Cognito I | 100 | 2.9187440 |\n| 229 | 1 | SOTA Push: Final ASN Refinement of 32-Start SLSQP | Cognito I | 99 | 2.9187440 |\n| 228 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Full Hybrid Seeding (Grid + Row + Farthest-Point) | Quest I | 98 | 2.9062145 |\n| 227 | 1 | Enhanced SLSQP Generator (32 Starts) for SOTA Push | Cognito I | 98 | 0.0320000 |\n| 226 |\
